  "problem": "The number of completed online course enrollments increases by $18$ enrollments every hour during a promotional event. What differential equation describes the rate of change of the number of enrollments $E(t)?$ Assume that the time $t$ is measured in hours.\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=$  \n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "If the number of enrollments is $E,$ then the rate of change of the number of enrollments is $\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t},$ where $t$ is the time in hours.\n\nSince $18$ new enrollments are added every hour, the rate of change of the number of enrollments is given by the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}E}{\\text{d}t}=18.\n$$",
